            <ArticleTitle>Giant hydronephrosis secondary to ureteropelvic junction obstruction in adults: report of a case and review of literatures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4715-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Giant hydronephrosis is rare to be seen in adults. Herein, we report a case of a 20-year-old male referred for abdominal pain. A radiological study revealed a giant left hydronephrosis. Nephrectomy was performed. During the operation, the ureteropelvic junction obstruction position was revealed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
